  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 520.02 Application for Walking Disability Plates or Placards by an Individual",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 520.02 Application for Walking Disability Plates or Placards by an Individual.\n\n(a) Pursuant to RSA 261:88, an applicant for a walking disability plate or placard shall complete the prescribed form.\n\n(b) An applicant for a walking disability plate or placard shall furnish the following on the prescribed form:\n\n(1) Name, address, and date of birth;\n\n(2) Whether the request is for walking disability plates, walking disability vanity plates, or a placard; and\n\n(3) Certification by a licensed physician, physician assistant, podiatrist, or advanced practice registered nurse, pursuant to the requirements set forth in Saf-C 520.01.\n\n(c) Each applicant shall sign and date the form under penalty of unsworn falsification.\n\n(d) If the applicant is requesting a walking disability plate, they shall submit a photocopy of their current certificate of registration along with the prescribed form.\n\nSource. #7069, eff 8-5-99 (formerly Saf-C 518, see Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 500); ss by #8999, eff 9-29-07; ss by #10135, eff 5-23-12; ss by #13521, eff 1-13-23 (formerly Saf-C 521.03)",
